<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91288" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωχ-εύω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-σω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.309
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωχεύεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.2
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be a beggar, go begging</i>, Il.cc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὰ δῆμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.73
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				10.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				921
			</span></i> (anap.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ξενίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.2.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be as poor as a beggar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				322
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Erx.</u>
				394b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph. c.
			gen., <i>to be badly off for</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραγμάτων</span>, of historians, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				7.7.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>beg</i> (<i>for</i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῖτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.pers.,
				<i>ask an alms of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					922
				</span></i>
			.</div>
